thub.com/users/SteveXiSong/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveXiSong/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveXiSong/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2022-05-20T22:06:59Z","updated_at":"2022-09-20T06:19:52Z","closed_at":"2022-05-26T18:52:24Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-467](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-467)\r\n### Description\n\nIn our mem_tracker.h, YB uses TCMalloc properties to retrieve the actual heap usage.\r\nThe current calculation for `GetTCMallocActualHeapSizeBytes()` is not accurate. As pointed in the original TCMalloc [header](https://github.com/google/tcmalloc/blob/master/tcmalloc/malloc_extension.h#L226), the `generic.heap_size` doesn't include `tcmalloc.pageheap_unmapped_bytes`. So subtracting 'tcmalloc.pageheap_unmapped_bytes' doesn't make any sense.\r\nRegarding that we want to calculate the actual physical (sort of) usage in the heap, just simply use `generic.heap_size`.","closed_by":{"login":"SteveXiSong","id":5407809,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MDc4MDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5407809?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveXiSong","html_url":"https://github.com/SteveXiSong","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveXiSong/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveXiSong/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveXiSong/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveXiSong/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveXiSong/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveXiSong/orgs","